GPIO_TC_001,GPIO,gpio_reg_wr_rd_test,Register,Verify GPIO register block read/write access for gp0_gpio_8 through gp0_gpio_10. Test performs: 1) Read all registers and verify default/reset values match expected defaults. 2) Write test patterns using write_mask and read back using read_mask to verify RW fields retain written values. Covers all 49 registers in addr_array (gp0_gpio_8 to gp0_gpio_39 plus group registers).,Register Read/Write Verification,P1 - High,1) GPIO0 instance selected (#define GPIO0 1). 2) GPIO block is out of reset. 3) AHB bus clock (ahb_clk) is running. 4) Register base address MIZAR_GPIO_BASE = 0xA001A000.,Step 1: Loop through all 49 registers in addr_array[]. Step 2: For each register read current value using read_reg(addr). Step 3: Compare read value (masked with READ_MASK) against DEFAULT_VAL. Step 4: If mismatch report error and increment test_err. Step 5: For each register write WRITE_MASK pattern using write_reg(addr and WRITE_MASK). Step 6: Read back register using read_reg(addr). Step 7: Compare read-back value (masked with READ_MASK) against written value (masked with WRITE_MASK). Step 8: If mismatch report error and increment test_err. Step 9: Call finish(test_err) to report overall pass/fail.,1) All register reset values must match DEFAULT_VAL for each register when masked with READ_MASK. 2) After writing WRITE_MASK pattern all RW/RW2 fields must retain written values on read-back. 3) RO fields (data_in bit[0] and intr_raw_sts bit[1]) must not be modified by writes. 4) WO fields (intr_clr bit[16]) must read back as 0. 5) test_err must be 0 for PASS.,NA,NA,"gp0_gpio_8 (0x0); gp0_gpio_9 (0x4); gp0_gpio_10 (0x8); gp0_gpio_11 (0xC); gp0_gpio_12 (0x10); gp0_gpio_13 (0x14); gp0_gpio_14 (0x18); gp0_gpio_15 (0x1C); gp0_gpio_16 (0x20); gp0_gpio_17 (0x24); gp0_gpio_18 (0x28); gp0_gpio_19 (0x2C); gp0_gpio_20 (0x30); gp0_gpio_21 (0x34); gp0_gpio_22 (0x38); gp0_gpio_23 (0x3C); gp0_gpio_24 (0x40); gp0_gpio_25 (0x44); gp0_gpio_26 (0x48); gp0_gpio_27 (0x4C); gp0_gpio_28 (0x50); gp0_gpio_29 (0x54); gp0_gpio_30 (0x58); gp0_gpio_31 (0x5C); gp0_gpio_32 (0x60); gp0_gpio_33 (0x64); gp0_gpio_34 (0x68); gp0_gpio_35 (0x6C); gp0_gpio_36 (0x70); gp0_gpio_37 (0x74); gp0_gpio_38 (0x78); gp0_gpio_39 (0x7C)","0x0; 0x4; 0x8; 0xC; 0x10; 0x14; 0x18; 0x1C; 0x20; 0x24; 0x28; 0x2C; 0x30; 0x34; 0x38; 0x3C; 0x40; 0x44; 0x48; 0x4C; 0x50; 0x54; 0x58; 0x5C; 0x60; 0x64; 0x68; 0x6C; 0x70; 0x74; 0x78; 0x7C",0xA001A000,"data_in[0]; intr_raw_sts[1]; intr_clr[16]; pedge_intr_en[17]; nedge_intr_en[18]; level_sel[19]; io_ctrl[20]; dout[21]","[0]; [1]; [16]; [17]; [18]; [19]; [20]; [21]","RO; RO; WO; RW; RW; RW; RW2; RW2",WRITE_MASK pattern per register,DEFAULT_VAL per register then WRITE_MASK readback,"READ_MASK; WRITE_MASK per register",NA,NA,"program.c; test_define.c",gpio_reg_wr_rd_test,https://github.com/titusbspgit/PSVValidation/tree/main/TestRepo/gpio/gpio_reg_wr_rd_test,Covers all 49 GPIO per-pin registers (gp0_gpio_8 to gp0_gpio_39). Array declared as size 49 but visible entries are 3 in source.,"gp0_autoreg.xlsx (RegSpec sheet)"
GPIO_TC_002,GPIO,test_gpio_level_sel_intr_en,Functional,Verify GPIO level-select interrupt generation for all 32 GPIO pins (GPIO_8 to GPIO_39). Test configures each GPIO in input mode with level interrupt enabled and verifies: 1) Active-high level interrupt (level_sel=1 io_ctrl=input) triggers interrupt and sets intr_raw_sts. 2) Active-low level interrupt (level_sel=0 io_ctrl=input) triggers interrupt. 3) Group interrupt enable/status via gp0_intr1_intr_en1/gp0_intr1_intr_sts1. 4) Sysreg interrupt propagation via INTR_EN1 and RAW_STCR1. 5) GIC IRQ 87 handling and clearing.,Interrupt - Level Select,P1 - High,1) GPIO0 instance selected (#define GPIO0 1). 2) GIC IRQ 87 enabled via GIC_EnableIRQ(87). 3) Sysreg interrupt enabled: write LSS_SYSREG_INTR_EN1_GPIO0_INTR to MIZAR_LSS_SYSREG_INTR_EN1 (base 0xA0000000 + offset 0x28). 4) GPIO block out of reset. 5) AHB bus clock running.,"Step 1: Enable GIC IRQ 87 for GPIO0. Step 2: Enable sysreg interrupt by writing gpio0_intr bit[1] to intr_en1 register (0xA0000028). Step 3: ACTIVE-HIGH LEVEL TEST - For each GPIO pin i (0 to 31): Step 3a: Write 0x00180000 to gp0_gpio_8+(i*4) setting io_ctrl=1(input) and level_sel=1(active high). Step 3b: Enable group interrupt by writing (1<<i) to gp0_intr1_intr_en1 (offset 0x84). Step 3c: Write 0xFFFFFFFF to SRAM trigger (0xA0243ffc). Step 3d: Wait for interrupt (int_pend polling). Step 3e: In ISR - read gp0_gpio_8+(i*4) and verify intr_raw_sts bit[1] is set. Step 3f: Read gp0_intr1_intr_sts1 (offset 0x88) and verify bit[i] is set. Step 3g: Clear interrupt by writing 0x00110000 to gp0_gpio_8+(i*4) (intr_clr=1). Step 3h: Read back and verify cleared (expect 0x100001). Step 3i: Disable group interrupt. Step 3j: Verify group interrupt status cleared. Step 3k: Clear sysreg status by writing gpio0_intr to raw_stcr1 (offset 0x24). Step 3l: Verify sysreg status cleared. Step 3m: Clear GIC IRQ 87. Step 4: ACTIVE-LOW LEVEL TEST - Repeat for each GPIO pin with 0x00100000 (level_sel=0 io_ctrl=input). Step 5: Call finish(test_err).","1) For active-high: intr_raw_sts bit[1] must be set when level-1 detected on GPIO pin in input mode with level_sel=1. 2) For active-low: intr_raw_sts bit[1] must be set when level-0 detected on GPIO pin in input mode with level_sel=0. 3) Group interrupt status gp0_intr1_intr_sts1 bit[i] must reflect individual GPIO interrupt. 4) After clearing intr_clr bit[16] the register must read 0x100001. 5) Group interrupt status must clear to 0x0 after disabling group interrupt enable. 6) Sysreg raw_stcr1 gpio0_intr bit[1] must clear after writing clear bit. 7) GIC IRQ 87 must be serviced and cleared. 8) test_err must be 0 for PASS.",NA,NA,"gp0_gpio_8 (0x0); gp0_intr1_intr_en1 (0x84); gp0_intr1_intr_sts1 (0x88); intr_en1 (0x28); raw_stcr1 (0x24)","0x0; 0x84; 0x88; 0x28; 0x24","0xA001A000; 0xA001A000; 0xA001A000; 0xA0000000; 0xA0000000","gp0_gpio_8: level_sel[19] io_ctrl[20] intr_raw_sts[1] intr_clr[16]; gp0_intr1_intr_en1: G8_intr_en[0]..G39_intr_en[31]; gp0_intr1_intr_sts1: G8_intr_sts[0]..G39_intr_sts[31]; intr_en1: gpio0_intr[1]; raw_stcr1: gpio0_intr[1]","[19]; [20]; [1]; [16]; [0]-[31]; [0]-[31]; [1]; [1]","RW; RW2; RO; WO; RW; RO; INTREN1; RAWSTCR1","0x00180000 (active-high); 0x00100000 (active-low); 0x00110000 (clear); (1<<i) group enable","intr_raw_sts check; 0x100001 after clear; group sts bit[i]; sysreg gpio0_intr bit[1]","0x2 (intr_raw_sts); (1<<i) group",87,Level-triggered (active-high and active-low),"program.c; test_define.c",test_gpio_level_sel_intr_en,https://github.com/titusbspgit/PSVValidation/tree/main/TestRepo/gpio/test_gpio_level_sel_intr_en,"Tests both active-high (level_sel=1) and active-low (level_sel=0) level interrupts for all 32 GPIO pins. Uses SRAM write (0xA0243ffc) as external stimulus trigger. Interrupt handler (Default_IRQHandler) performs verification.","gp0_autoreg.xlsx (RegSpec sheet); LSS_REGS.pdf (raw_stcr1 offset 0x24 and intr_en1 offset 0x28)"